[[:db/retract 17592186102126 :answer-field/choices 17592186102128] [:db/retract 17592186102126 :answer-field/choices 17592186102129] [:db/retract 17592186102126 :answer-field/choices 17592186102130] [:db/retract 17592186102126 :answer-field/choices 17592186102131] [:db/retract 17592186102126 :answer-field/choices 17592186102127] [:db/retract 17592186102144 :answer-field/choices 17592186102145] [:db/retract 17592186102144 :answer-field/choices 17592186102146] [:db/retract 17592186102144 :answer-field/choices 17592186102147] [:db/retract 17592186102144 :answer-field/choices 17592186102148] [:db/retract 17592186102144 :answer-field/choices 17592186102149] {:db/id 17592186105855 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-79ef7418-2499-5a5e-9753-d6a82e3d1195" "question-78d41512-3eb5-5609-aad8-a61279c74c85"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106040 :question/problem "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$" :question/worked-solution "For convenience, we express $r(t)$ in column vector notation:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102126 :answer-field/correct "answer-acdafd0f-04a3-50f3-9016-229636fea9cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c37312e-1d93-53a0-ba9c-7e273739a5c3" "answer-0acdd021-7840-54cb-948b-ea5f4720bcd9" "answer-e4176979-2302-53d4-9836-168bdc17d4a0" "answer-acdafd0f-04a3-50f3-9016-229636fea9cb" "answer-554fb461-f8fc-5f02-8c53-5d662d712545"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c37312e-1d93-53a0-ba9c-7e273739a5c3" :answer/id #uuid "7c37312e-1d93-53a0-ba9c-7e273739a5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0acdd021-7840-54cb-948b-ea5f4720bcd9" :answer/id #uuid "0acdd021-7840-54cb-948b-ea5f4720bcd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4176979-2302-53d4-9836-168bdc17d4a0" :answer/id #uuid "e4176979-2302-53d4-9836-168bdc17d4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acdafd0f-04a3-50f3-9016-229636fea9cb" :answer/id #uuid "acdafd0f-04a3-50f3-9016-229636fea9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-554fb461-f8fc-5f02-8c53-5d662d712545" :answer/id #uuid "554fb461-f8fc-5f02-8c53-5d662d712545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105856 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7df57c40-4642-538c-b446-11650ad2af53"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7df57c40-4642-538c-b446-11650ad2af53" :question/id #uuid "7df57c40-4642-538c-b446-11650ad2af53" :question/math-academy-id "q-126916" :question/problem "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*" :question/worked-solution "For convenience, we express $r(t)$ in column vector notation:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, *negatively* oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented clockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *counterclockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f82b12c-6ce8-5ff6-b513-2e1efd6f0437"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f82b12c-6ce8-5ff6-b513-2e1efd6f0437" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f82b12c-6ce8-5ff6-b513-2e1efd6f0437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5c95c20-8a83-5b7f-a94b-48be5207dcd9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5f1e04e-c989-540c-945e-5530f0a9ef5d" "answer-ebba1cbb-de04-5f96-928a-2186ab923ede" "answer-4e0f7628-1647-5244-8346-f685935b3b5d" "answer-b5c95c20-8a83-5b7f-a94b-48be5207dcd9" "answer-07f0b6be-b8a6-509c-9eef-fddd1e4c52cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5f1e04e-c989-540c-945e-5530f0a9ef5d" :answer/id #uuid "b5f1e04e-c989-540c-945e-5530f0a9ef5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebba1cbb-de04-5f96-928a-2186ab923ede" :answer/id #uuid "ebba1cbb-de04-5f96-928a-2186ab923ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e0f7628-1647-5244-8346-f685935b3b5d" :answer/id #uuid "4e0f7628-1647-5244-8346-f685935b3b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5c95c20-8a83-5b7f-a94b-48be5207dcd9" :answer/id #uuid "b5c95c20-8a83-5b7f-a94b-48be5207dcd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07f0b6be-b8a6-509c-9eef-fddd1e4c52cd" :answer/id #uuid "07f0b6be-b8a6-509c-9eef-fddd1e4c52cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106043 :question/problem "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*" :question/worked-solution "For convenience, we express $r(t)$ in column vector notation:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, *negatively* oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented clockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *counterclockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102144 :answer-field/correct "answer-fd95b973-cef8-59e2-935c-7fcafbf777f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bde73f4-acbe-5a30-bd8d-32583815fc67" "answer-da1537f7-60f2-5487-98fb-d8eb37445eb8" "answer-e881b58b-f16e-577e-bb7a-de715dbd1a37" "answer-8a98e20c-8619-5648-a5cf-3ffe0e3b9b41" "answer-fd95b973-cef8-59e2-935c-7fcafbf777f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bde73f4-acbe-5a30-bd8d-32583815fc67" :answer/id #uuid "6bde73f4-acbe-5a30-bd8d-32583815fc67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da1537f7-60f2-5487-98fb-d8eb37445eb8" :answer/id #uuid "da1537f7-60f2-5487-98fb-d8eb37445eb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e881b58b-f16e-577e-bb7a-de715dbd1a37" :answer/id #uuid "e881b58b-f16e-577e-bb7a-de715dbd1a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a98e20c-8619-5648-a5cf-3ffe0e3b9b41" :answer/id #uuid "8a98e20c-8619-5648-a5cf-3ffe0e3b9b41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd95b973-cef8-59e2-935c-7fcafbf777f7" :answer/id #uuid "fd95b973-cef8-59e2-935c-7fcafbf777f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-79ef7418-2499-5a5e-9753-d6a82e3d1195" :question/id #uuid "79ef7418-2499-5a5e-9753-d6a82e3d1195" :question/math-academy-id "q-149680" :question/problem "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$" :question/worked-solution "For convenience, we express $r(t)$ in column vector notation:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2487de5-11c9-540d-8192-d573aee45967"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2487de5-11c9-540d-8192-d573aee45967" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2487de5-11c9-540d-8192-d573aee45967" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c5bdb73-6898-56ac-bbfd-188b444b01de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3065874e-f894-5c1a-a03f-26e6b2e6c08a" "answer-7dc69b79-8fb8-593f-825a-4bbd5ae3ad91" "answer-5c5bdb73-6898-56ac-bbfd-188b444b01de" "answer-6f4d0844-3d2a-5a55-ac0a-b06e2d2a8f44" "answer-fad75c53-910c-59f2-aa27-ab56b7a5017d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3065874e-f894-5c1a-a03f-26e6b2e6c08a" :answer/id #uuid "3065874e-f894-5c1a-a03f-26e6b2e6c08a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dc69b79-8fb8-593f-825a-4bbd5ae3ad91" :answer/id #uuid "7dc69b79-8fb8-593f-825a-4bbd5ae3ad91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c5bdb73-6898-56ac-bbfd-188b444b01de" :answer/id #uuid "5c5bdb73-6898-56ac-bbfd-188b444b01de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f4d0844-3d2a-5a55-ac0a-b06e2d2a8f44" :answer/id #uuid "6f4d0844-3d2a-5a55-ac0a-b06e2d2a8f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fad75c53-910c-59f2-aa27-ab56b7a5017d" :answer/id #uuid "fad75c53-910c-59f2-aa27-ab56b7a5017d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78d41512-3eb5-5609-aad8-a61279c74c85" :question/id #uuid "78d41512-3eb5-5609-aad8-a61279c74c85" :question/math-academy-id "q-149681" :question/problem "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$" :question/worked-solution "For convenience, we express $r(t)$ in column vector notation:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ee2b7e94-139d-52df-a733-a979d04555a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ee2b7e94-139d-52df-a733-a979d04555a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee2b7e94-139d-52df-a733-a979d04555a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-322819d7-8ec8-5e47-8eb6-5ed5edaa65a1" "answer-12c2611f-f075-5bef-9b12-8e6d7c6016ce" "answer-21912693-46e5-54c5-885b-ffece0e4f4ab" "answer-b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" "answer-d0954837-8233-5864-88b9-32dce2d50d2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-322819d7-8ec8-5e47-8eb6-5ed5edaa65a1" :answer/id #uuid "322819d7-8ec8-5e47-8eb6-5ed5edaa65a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12c2611f-f075-5bef-9b12-8e6d7c6016ce" :answer/id #uuid "12c2611f-f075-5bef-9b12-8e6d7c6016ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21912693-46e5-54c5-885b-ffece0e4f4ab" :answer/id #uuid "21912693-46e5-54c5-885b-ffece0e4f4ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" :answer/id #uuid "b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0954837-8233-5864-88b9-32dce2d50d2f" :answer/id #uuid "d0954837-8233-5864-88b9-32dce2d50d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-be844a0b-1b21-5bf9-af56-f92614fa7bb7" :activity/id #uuid "be844a0b-1b21-5bf9-af56-f92614fa7bb7" :activity/title "Outward-Pointing Unit Normal Vectors in 2D" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050104 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-091b59dd-5e66-5d54-a04a-5e006f7a4412" "step-01d78fae-df26-523a-a169-023a86387db3" "step-a61f17a9-02c9-5d8f-bc89-f080656ef9f3" "step-c3c4339d-e499-5428-8be7-e53653cc5d16" "step-792a52ce-5964-52dd-90b1-8b9d723859c6"] :activity/first-step "step-091b59dd-5e66-5d54-a04a-5e006f7a4412" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-091b59dd-5e66-5d54-a04a-5e006f7a4412" :step/id #uuid "091b59dd-5e66-5d54-a04a-5e006f7a4412" :step/content 17592186106040 :step/next "step-01d78fae-df26-523a-a169-023a86387db3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-01d78fae-df26-523a-a169-023a86387db3" :step/id #uuid "01d78fae-df26-523a-a169-023a86387db3" :step/content "question-7df57c40-4642-538c-b446-11650ad2af53" :step/next "step-a61f17a9-02c9-5d8f-bc89-f080656ef9f3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a61f17a9-02c9-5d8f-bc89-f080656ef9f3" :step/id #uuid "a61f17a9-02c9-5d8f-bc89-f080656ef9f3" :step/content 17592186106043 :step/next "step-c3c4339d-e499-5428-8be7-e53653cc5d16" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c3c4339d-e499-5428-8be7-e53653cc5d16" :step/id #uuid "c3c4339d-e499-5428-8be7-e53653cc5d16" :step/content "question-79ef7418-2499-5a5e-9753-d6a82e3d1195" :step/next "step-792a52ce-5964-52dd-90b1-8b9d723859c6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-792a52ce-5964-52dd-90b1-8b9d723859c6" :step/id #uuid "792a52ce-5964-52dd-90b1-8b9d723859c6" :step/content "question-78d41512-3eb5-5609-aad8-a61279c74c85" :db/ensure [:step/va